   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div style=\"overflow:auto\"><div style=\"max-height:10000px\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Roboto,arial,sans-serif;line-height:18px\">Dear all,<br>I would like to get a covariance matrix out of a correlation matrix (12 times 12, therefore the sd vector also has 12 entries) with &quot;cor2cov(cor.mat = cor.matrix, sd = sd.vector)&quot; from the MBESS package and I get the error message &quot;The object &#39;cor.mat&#39; should be either a symmetric or a triangular matrix&quot;, but my matrix is symmetric. When I run lavaan with &quot;<span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);line-height:normal;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">cor2cov(R = cor.matrix, sds = <a href=\"http://vector.sd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://vector.sd&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792429791656000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1VST8y3uhl9v8_fvu_UCzr\">vector.sd</a>)&quot; I get the error message &quot;unbenutze argumente&quot;. </span></div><div style=\"color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Roboto,arial,sans-serif;line-height:18px\">What have I done wrong? Do you have any idea?<br>Thx a lot!﻿</div></div></div></div></div><div></div><div></div></div><div><div></div></div><div><div><div style=\"display:inline-block\"></div><div></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tkcr_NWaxE4J",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2015-07-06T14:06:09Z",
   "subject": "Re: Error Message: The object cor.mat should be either a symmetric or a triangular matrix",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">It is hard to tell what is going wrong without being able to reproduce the problem.  Can you provide the matrix and vector that lead to the error?  <div><br></div><div>My first guess is that the object &quot;cor.matrix&quot; is not stored as a matrix, or perhaps was imported as character rather than numeric.  You might get some useful information by running :<div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">class(cor.matrix)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">mode(cor.matrix)</font><div><br></div></div><div>Terry</div><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
