  {
   "id": "NngV9FYp7pYJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2015-07-07T09:55:14Z",
   "subject": "Re: Error Message: The object cor.mat should be either a symmetric or a triangular matrix",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">This looks fine to me.  Thanks for including a visual prinout of your matrix, but again, it is hard for anyone on the forum to find out what is wrong without being able to reproduce the problem.  I pasted your information and read it into R (version 3.2.1), and I only included rownames for the matrix, not column names (as I saw in your output).  I also got an error message when I used the MBESS function, and the reason is that your correlation matrix doesn&#39;t pass the test for being symmetric (if you imported the correlations from a file, there might be a typo in your data):<div><br></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">&gt; isSymmetric(cor.matrix)</font></div></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">[1] FALSE</font></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>But when I used the lavaan (version 0.5-19.863) function <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">cor2cov()</font> it worked fine for me (see output below signature).  <div><br></div><div>I did notice that in your original message, you referred to an object &quot;<span style=\"color:rgb(64,64,64);font-family:Roboto,arial,sans-serif;line-height:18px\">sd.vector</span>&quot; using the MBESS function, but you referred to an object &quot;<a href=\"http://vector.sd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://vector.sd&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792429791666000&amp;usg=AOvVaw27kYmrDubeYtfcwsQxgWkY\">vector.sd</a>&quot; using the lavaan function.  This won&#39;t work unless <a href=\"http://vector.sd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://vector.sd&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792429791666000&amp;usg=AOvVaw27kYmrDubeYtfcwsQxgWkY\">vector.sd</a> == sd.vector.  </div><div><br></div><div>But the reason for your error message is exactly what it says: you included unused arguments.  That doesn&#39;t seem to make sense because &quot;R&quot; and &quot;sds&quot; are existing arguments for the lavaan function.  Therefore, I think that when you called &quot;<font face=\"courier new, monospace\">cor2cov</font>&quot;, it was using the MBESS function (perhaps because MBESS was loaded into your workspace after lavaan was).  It will probably work if you tell R to use the lavaan version of that function:</div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">lavaan::cor2cov(R = cor.matrix, sds = sd.vector)</font><br></div><div><br></div><div>This is why a complete R script to reproduce your problem is always more helpful than a verbal description alone.</div><div><div><br></div><div>Terry</div><div><br></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">&gt; round(sd.vector, 4)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> [1] 0.3002 0.2999 0.3005 0.2998 0.3004 0.3000 0.3001 0.3002 0.2998 0.3002 0.3001 0.3003</font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">&gt; round(cor.matrix, 3)</span><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
